SetAmount_Budgets_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when a call into Budgets is already running
│   └── it should revert with ReentrantCall
├── when the budget does not exist
│   └── it should revert with UnknownBudget
├── when the budget is a top budget and the caller is not its Safe
│   └── it should revert with NotAuthorised
├── when the budget is a child and the caller is not authorised for its parent
│   └── it should revert with NotAuthorised
├── given the caller wears only the budget's own hat
│   └── it should revert with NotAuthorised
└── when the caller may set it
    ├── when the new amount is below own spend plus ownCommitted plus childrenAmount
    │   └── it should revert with AmountBelowUse with what the budget uses
    ├── given a pending scheduled payment holds part of what the budget uses
    │   └── it should revert with AmountBelowUse until the payment is cancelled or paid
    ├── given an ended agreement still holds its reservation until settled
    │   └── it should revert with AmountBelowUse until Agreements settle frees it
    ├── given the budget's period turned since it was last used
    │   └── it should count its own spend as 0
    ├── when the budget is a child and the raise is more than the room left in the parent
    │   └── it should revert with ChildrenExceedParent
    └── when the new amount fits
        ├── it should set the amount
        ├── given the budget is a child
        │   └── it should move the parent's childrenAmount by the difference
        ├── given the new amount equals exactly what the budget uses
        │   └── it should set it and leave nothing to spend
        ├── given the budget is closed
        │   └── it should still set the amount
        └── it should emit BudgetAmountSet
